    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0115" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.154/3266</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-11">October 11, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Warren<anchor n="9" xml:id="d109-f1"/> came in to pay his respects. He stated
                    that the Inter-American Highway<anchor n="10" xml:id="d109-f2"/> financed with
                    Lend-Lease funds was not going well. He also informed me of the changed
                    conditions resulting in there now being very little reason for the road, and
                    that Haiti and the Dominican Republic are not interested. He feels that unless
                    there are impelling military reasons for its construction it should not
                    proceed.</p>
                <p>I have informed Mr. Bernhard Knollenberg of Lend-Lease of this.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d109-f1" n="9" xml:id="d109-f1-content">
                <p>Avra M. Warren, Ambassador in the Dominican Republic.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d109-f2" n="10" xml:id="d109-f2-content">
                <p>Caribbean land-water route.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
